&lt;p&gt;You will be focused on validating and architecting package and system-level test strategies for high-speed I/O interfaces on Lightmatter’s novel product line. In this role, you will be responsible for setting up and executing high-speed electrical characterization, driving link bring-ups, and stress-testing I/Os in system environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with cross-functional teams to transition these technologies into high-volume manufacturing. We are looking for an engineer with a proven track record of testing real-world industry products. You will be part of a growing interdisciplinary team with a lot of opportunities to learn and make a big impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute high-speed serial I/O characterization and validation across multiple platforms for Lightmatter products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with architecture, signal integrity, and silicon design teams to understand the technology and conceptualize characterization and test techniques targeting product manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect test concepts, test platforms, and design-for-test rules, providing critical feedback during the technology concept phase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up and operate a wide range of high-speed lab equipment, including oscilloscopes, BERTs, AWGs, TDRs, and VNAs/PNAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop Python-based test software and scripts to automate lab measurements, test execution, data analysis, and parameter extraction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and develop stress testing methodologies to identify design operating limits of serial I/Os post-system integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and triage complex issues with compliance test hardware, fixtures, software, and the Device Under Test (DUT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with vendors to specify and procure state-of-the-art test equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of industry experience in transceiver, SerDes, or high-speed link test development on products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive hands-on lab experience and familiarity with high-speed equipment, including oscilloscopes, BERTs, PPGs, VNAs, and spectrum analyzers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong familiarity with high-speed interfaces and analog building blocks (e.g., PLL, CDR, CTLE, DFE, FFE, and FEC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in test system automation and data processing using Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and debugging skills to identify and solve hardware and signal integrity issues during the testing process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to convey complex technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
