&lt;p&gt;Lightmatter is (re)inventing the future of computing with light!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Electrical Design Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Electrical Design Engineer to contribute to the development of the next generation of silicon photonics based artificial intelligence accelerators and interconnect products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead board and system solutions that leverage Lightmatter’s technology to enable advanced machine learning, artificial intelligence, and large-scale interconnect platforms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead and own HW systems efforts, collaborate closely with teams across hardware and software, including mechanical, packaging, and IC engineering, to design, integrate, troubleshoot and release system-level products at the leading edge of innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the system architect and technical leads to define system-level hardware requirements and spec&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical design of power, memory, and interconnect circuits, working in both the analog and digital domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify electrical and optical components to fit the application based on specifications provided by the IC and photonics engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Starting from fundamental concepts and system considerations you will develop conceptual designs, physical modeling, and simulations of chip-modules and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and review PCB layout designs, providing complete and detailed electrical constraint rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the board and system is manufacturable to the latest technologies with high yield and robustness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualification of chip and system electrical properties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform laboratory validation of boards and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead integration with mechanical, software, IC, and other related teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support contract manufacturing during prototype and production phase to resolve any issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with component vendors and other supply partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research new components, processes, and technologies to meet product goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree in Electrical Engineering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of related experience in system-level electrical design, having successfully taken several products from concept to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in schematic design using Cadence, Mentor, or Altium tool set (Altium preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In depth knowledge on VRMs, high speed SERDES, CPUs and various interfaces/protocols such as PCIe, Ethernet, QSPI, I3C, I2C, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in lab experimentation, non-intrusive circuit debugging, and leading cross-functional integration teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working with thermal solutions for integrated circuits and their board level systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Product Lifecycle Management tools, e.g. Oracle Agile, Arena, or Omnify PLM with an understanding of BOM and ECO management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing electrical systems for networking or similar industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of integrated circuit layout, and designing a carrier PCBA for it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of common manufacturing and design processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Systems Engineering principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with 3D Mechanical CAD tools, e.g. Solidworks or AutoCAD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
