&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lightmatter is leading the revolution in AI data center infrastructure, enabling the next giant leaps in human progress. The company invented the world’s first 3D-stacked photonics engine, Passage™, capable of connecting thousands to millions of processors at the speed of light in extreme-scale data centers for the most advanced AI and HPC workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lightmatter raised $400 million in its Series D round, reaching a valuation of $4.4 billion. We will continue to accelerate the development of data center photonics and grow every department at Lightmatter!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about tackling complex challenges, making an impact, and being an expert in your craft, join our team of brilliant scientists, engineers, and accomplished industry leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lightmatter is (re)inventing the future of computing with light!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About this Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a motivated, dedicated, and hands-on mechanical design engineer to help develop a chassis and rack platforms for the next-generation artificial intelligence server alongside a team of world-class scientists and engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mechanical Engineer at Lightmatter, you will sit at the critical intersection of silicon photonics, advanced 3D packaging, and extreme-density thermal management. You won&#39;t just be tweaking existing designs; you will be the practical execution engine transforming complex electro-optical concepts into scalable, manufacturable hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this role focuses on flawless technical execution rather than top-level project architecture, your hands-on impact will be immense. You will navigate the transition from initial CAD and prototype builds to leading external Contract Manufacturers (CMs). If you are a rigorous, detail-oriented engineer eager to solve complex thermal-mechanical packaging puzzles, orchestrate supply chains, and build the physical backbone of next-generation AI infrastructure, we want you on our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, test, analyze, integrate, qualify and document hardware of moderate to high complexity, in a dynamic startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure proper packaging of optical, electrical and related components for optimal thermal performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for mechanical design from generating CAD and drawings, to BOM generation and crafting work instructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully understand project requirements and timelines while identifying gaps and drive to closure with the stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate and drive design reviews while managing the resulting feedback and change requests.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate in root-cause-analysis and technical investigations with&amp;nbsp; cross-functional teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Drive hands-on in-house build and integration activities, scaling from initial prototype fabrication to leading external CMs for high-volume production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage outside fabricators to ensure correct build-to-print and quality workmanship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technical program managers to define a detailed timeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively mitigate and manage lead-time issues with the supply chain team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with relevant cross-functional engineering teams to understand dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide assistance to creating technical road-maps, establishing best practices, and determining product feasibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or related fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in system mechanical design with multiple successful product releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in a 3D CAD solid modeling software package such as SolidWorks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with both thermal and structural testing and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with state-of-the-art mechanical engineering design and analysis tools (ANSYS preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess a strong understanding in the application of heat transfer principles, strength of materials, materials selection, design for vibration environments and the ability to apply those principles to unique mechanical design challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in electronics packaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and adaptive in execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with 3D printing equipment and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with FEA software package (ANSYS, SolidWorks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with thermal simulation and analysis software package (IcePak, Flotherm)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
